(Summary, written by PutiaCNC)
(Spindle (!):            Not run by the program: it stops -M0- to ask you to start it at the)
(                        speed shown, and again before a tool change and at the end to stop it.)
(                        There is no work coordinate system: jog to the zero of the job and set)
(                        it with G92 X0 Y0 Z0 first.)
(Tools:                  1/4in compression bit, 1/4in ball nose. No tool change.)
(Pauses:                 The program stops 6 times with the spindle off: 'Start the spindle at)
(                        12000 rpm, then resume', 'Stop the spindle and change tool to 6.35 mm,)
(                        then touch off Z 0 and resume', 'Start the spindle at 10000 rpm, then)
(                        resume', 'Stop the spindle and change tool to 6 mm, then touch off Z 0)
(                        and resume', 'Start the spindle at 10000 rpm, then resume', 'Stop the)
(                        spindle, then resume'. Resume it when you are ready; the spindle)
(                        starts again by itself.)
(Cutting:                Down to Z -6 mm. 8450 mm of cutting, about 17 min 34 s in all.)
(End:                    Lifts to Z 5 mm, goes to X0 Y0.)
; PutiaCNC - Marlin (no spindle control)
; Stock 90 x 90 x 12 mm; XY0 = lower-left corner of stock, Z0 = top surface
G21 G90
; Marlin: jog the tool to the zero of the job and set it there with G92 X0 Y0 Z0 before you run this file
; Spindle: by hand. The program stops to ask you to start and stop it
G0 Z5
; Tool: 1/4in compression bit
M0 Start the spindle at 12000 rpm, then resume
